title: The Railway Strike
subtitle: The trains stop, and Ebert forbids the strike by decree.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 2
max-visits: 1

= The Railway Strike

On 1 February the railway officials of the Reich walk out. Their salaries are worth half what they were a year ago. By the evening almost nothing moves between Hamburg and Munich, and President Ebert signs a decree that forbids officials to strike. In Berlin the gas, water and tram workers come out in sympathy. The union federation keeps out of it.

The strikers are not communists. Most of them vote for the Centre or the SPD.

- @solidarity: Bring the Berlin works out beside them.
- @unions: Press the unions to back them.
- @quiet: Keep out of it.

@solidarity
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A strike in Berlin, and the railwaymen will remember who came.
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('councils');
RG.startStrike('berlin');
RG.district('berlin', {militancy: 6, repression: 4});
Q.e22_railway = 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Our cells bring out a few thousand men at Siemens and the AEG. The officials' leaders settle on 7 February. Our strikers go back with nothing, and the depot men at Lichtenberg buy them a round.

@unions
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Resolutions in a hundred branches. Slow, and the union men notice.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids work inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.against('union_work');
Q.e22_railway = 2;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The federation does not move. Its members have seen who stood up for the railwaymen.

@quiet
subtitle: No risk, and the strikers notice that too.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_railway = 0;
Q.worker_support -= 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 5;
!}

The Zentrale publishes a statement of sympathy. The strike ends after a week with a few concessions and many dismissals.
